00:30:08.400 --> 00:30:09.970
and more specific

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:13.210
conceptually,

00:30:13.210 --> 00:30:15.760
and to sort of help me follow through

00:30:15.760 --> 00:30:17.490
with a lot of my concepts in a way that

00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:18.990
I can't articulate right now at this

00:30:18.990 --> 00:30:20.020
time in the morning,

00:30:20.020 --> 00:30:25.020
but was I was asked and it
annoyed me basically why Asia.

00:30:26.100 --> 00:30:29.510
So of course there are histories
that are beyond the kind of

00:30:29.510 --> 00:30:33.400
bilateral West with one Asian country

00:30:33.400 --> 00:30:34.620
kind of traditional history Scots.

00:30:34.620 --> 00:30:36.050
So the Philippines and the US,

00:30:36.050 --> 00:30:37.210
the Philippines in Spain,

00:30:37.210 --> 00:30:39.653
France, and into China and et cetera.

00:30:40.600 --> 00:30:43.070
And they said, of course,

00:30:43.070 --> 00:30:44.580
there's a more complex world beyond that.

00:30:44.580 --> 00:30:45.413
So why?

00:30:45.413 --> 00:30:46.700
So then why Asia beyond that?

00:30:46.700 --> 00:30:49.831
And to me to have to explain
why you should be on that,

00:30:49.831 --> 00:30:53.040
then you would have to explain
why anywhere beyond that,

00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:55.250
it seems to me important enough

00:30:55.250 --> 00:30:58.170
that I don't have to think
it through even beyond that.

00:30:58.170 --> 00:31:00.690
But when pushed to do so,

00:31:00.690 --> 00:31:02.190
one thing that I thought that

00:31:02.190 --> 00:31:06.650
my history actually did bear out was

00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:10.430
and contribute was to
the history of the rise

00:31:10.430 --> 00:31:13.680
of the nation state as the political form

00:31:13.680 --> 00:31:16.720
over the course of the 20th century.

00:31:16.720 --> 00:31:21.720
And I think that it's an
interesting history because

00:31:22.400 --> 00:31:27.138
it shows the ways in which
the social Darwin is framework

00:31:27.138 --> 00:31:29.680
of the period amongst

00:31:31.240 --> 00:31:34.270
a lot of Asian actors

00:31:34.270 --> 00:31:36.480
made a kind of

00:31:38.220 --> 00:31:41.850
internationalist dualist kind
of formal experimentation

00:31:41.850 --> 00:31:44.293
seemed necessary and natural

00:31:44.293 --> 00:31:46.540
that your nationalism should be

00:31:46.540 --> 00:31:49.413
buttressed in a larger racial grouping.

00:31:50.890 --> 00:31:55.490
And I think that that
racialized interpretation

00:31:55.490 --> 00:31:57.680
of the international sphere

00:31:57.680 --> 00:32:01.110
will give us a fuller
understanding of modern Asia,

00:32:01.110 --> 00:32:04.320
as well as the Asia
within kind of Asianism

00:32:04.320 --> 00:32:05.880
and the ways in which
she was constituted both

00:32:05.880 --> 00:32:08.030
from and negotiate from
within and without.

00:32:09.080 --> 00:32:13.310
And I think that also what
you see in this history

00:32:13.310 --> 00:32:16.450
of the nation state is the ways in which

00:32:17.810 --> 00:32:21.110
it was globalized a lot
in the hands of Asians,

00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:24.360
but it is not nearly derivative of

00:32:25.300 --> 00:32:27.600
the Western form and the
Western history though,

00:32:27.600 --> 00:32:28.993
that was also under wait.

00:32:29.930 --> 00:32:34.020
You can also see through

00:32:34.020 --> 00:32:37.540
what I argue as a return to place

00:32:38.440 --> 00:32:41.960
the ways which those sort
of enlightenment ideals

00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:44.650
and the Western grammar
for the nation could seem

00:32:44.650 --> 00:32:49.259
insufficiently specific for as grounds

00:32:49.259 --> 00:32:52.950
for anti-colonial nationalism.

00:32:52.950 --> 00:32:57.140
And so return to sort of place

00:32:57.140 --> 00:33:00.697
as a kind of localized moveable plain,

00:33:00.697 --> 00:33:04.650
to counter that very
universal general plane,

00:33:04.650 --> 00:33:07.000
is an entry point where you can see

00:33:07.000 --> 00:33:10.860
the more specific in particular eyes,

00:33:10.860 --> 00:33:12.190
intellectual constructions,

00:33:12.190 --> 00:33:14.903
and world making and imaginings

00:33:14.903 --> 00:33:17.470
that are underway here to rather than be,

00:33:17.470 --> 00:33:20.760
are they just sort of
a transfer in migration

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:22.687
of this Western form of the nation

00:33:22.687 --> 00:33:25.143
and the nation state through Asia.

00:33:29.278 --> 00:33:33.120
And Southeast Asia in general I think

00:33:33.120 --> 00:33:35.760
bedevil's a lot of the assumptions about

00:33:35.760 --> 00:33:38.470
the history of the rise
of the nation state.

00:33:38.470 --> 00:33:39.700
On the one hand,

00:33:39.700 --> 00:33:43.170
it shows as my book does I think

00:33:44.100 --> 00:33:47.760
sort of the historical
viability of alternatives

00:33:47.760 --> 00:33:49.350
to the nation state on some level,

00:33:49.350 --> 00:33:51.660
even if not solely,

00:33:51.660 --> 00:33:53.890
but in sort of in concert with,

00:33:53.890 --> 00:33:55.270
but at the same time,

00:33:55.270 --> 00:33:58.970
it also shows a convergence
on the nation state.

00:33:58.970 --> 00:34:03.970
And so it's sort of good
if it doubles both as both

00:34:04.070 --> 00:34:04.903
sort of arguments,

00:34:04.903 --> 00:34:06.810
the prior argument of the literature,

00:34:06.810 --> 00:34:08.830
and then the current
argument of the literature.

00:34:08.830 --> 00:34:11.210
And so it's one of the
reasons why I think,

00:34:11.210 --> 00:34:12.490
as ever a Southeast Asia,

00:34:12.490 --> 00:34:15.210
it needs to be a stronger
part of the way we teach

00:34:15.210 --> 00:34:17.730
global history and
research global history,

00:34:17.730 --> 00:34:20.313
because it shakes up a
lot of our assumptions.

00:34:23.860 --> 00:34:26.110
- I love the way that you
described Southeast Asia

00:34:26.110 --> 00:34:28.873
