00:36:06.330 --> 00:36:09.140
- So one of the thinkers that

00:36:10.110 --> 00:36:13.720
a lot of the people I
studied references Plotkin

00:36:13.720 --> 00:36:18.160
and he talks about mutual
aid within a species

00:36:18.160 --> 00:36:21.990
as a sort of the tactic
for survival and necessity

00:36:21.990 --> 00:36:23.040
for survival.

00:36:23.040 --> 00:36:24.570
And this is one of the things that

00:36:24.570 --> 00:36:26.760
sort of bridges social Darwinism,

00:36:26.760 --> 00:36:28.670
and to punish aneurysm,

00:36:28.670 --> 00:36:31.873
is this idea of mutual
help within the species.

00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:35.530
More broadly I would say that

00:36:35.530 --> 00:36:38.730
the way social Darwinism is
originally theorized in Europe

00:36:38.730 --> 00:36:43.210
is as explaining sort of
difference in inequality

00:36:43.210 --> 00:36:44.940
within a nation,

00:36:44.940 --> 00:36:48.166
but the Asian thinkers that I look at

00:36:48.166 --> 00:36:52.810
treated as a way to explain
the difference between

00:36:52.810 --> 00:36:53.643
nation States

00:36:53.643 --> 00:36:54.890
within the international sphere

00:36:54.890 --> 00:36:59.050
and see it as a much
larger international amoral

00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:01.640
competition of survival.

00:37:01.640 --> 00:37:06.640
And I would say that the way
that it gets to the Filipinos

00:37:07.110 --> 00:37:09.330
is through a lot of the
European interlocutors

00:37:09.330 --> 00:37:10.370
that they have,

00:37:10.370 --> 00:37:14.220
the illustrators that I study
ended up studying in Germany

00:37:14.220 --> 00:37:17.170
and in Spain and in France.

00:37:17.170 --> 00:37:19.640
And they're very close to

00:37:22.080 --> 00:37:24.740
