00:41:42.233 --> 00:41:44.560
connects the Philippines to China,

00:41:44.560 --> 00:41:46.903
as far back as the second
century D at least,

00:41:47.790 --> 00:41:50.230
but in the history that
I'm looking at, though,

00:41:50.230 --> 00:41:51.810
there are very strong connections

00:41:51.810 --> 00:41:54.154
to Lenchishao and Sonia Said

00:41:54.154 --> 00:41:56.630
and they are very key figures within

00:41:56.630 --> 00:41:58.673
the sort of pan Asianism in motion,

00:41:59.881 --> 00:42:03.590
especially for the figure of
Marianna Pontus specifically.

00:42:03.590 --> 00:42:07.900
And they sort of hatch plans
together, the lend money,

00:42:07.900 --> 00:42:09.520
try it obtain arms,

00:42:09.520 --> 00:42:12.040
and try to enter into an agreement

00:42:12.040 --> 00:42:15.920
where they they share use of arms

00:42:15.920 --> 00:42:18.040
by lending a shared location

00:42:18.040 --> 00:42:20.590
in a certain sort of storage.

00:42:20.590 --> 00:42:22.640
So there's a lot of cooperation there.

00:42:22.640 --> 00:42:25.010
And I think that at least from

00:42:25.010 --> 00:42:27.260
my other points is specifically,

00:42:27.260 --> 00:42:29.750
they're very formative
to his understanding

00:42:29.750 --> 00:42:31.680
of the role that the Philippines Spain,

00:42:31.680 --> 00:42:34.880
within a modern Asia more generally,

00:42:34.880 --> 00:42:37.840
and help him sort of feel that

00:42:37.840 --> 00:42:39.530
the Philippines is leading the torch

00:42:39.530 --> 00:42:42.780
for the Malay race
liberate, the Malay race,

00:42:42.780 --> 00:42:45.030
and that he will play this role

00:42:45.030 --> 00:42:46.319
in the same way that Sonia Said

00:42:46.319 --> 00:42:47.833
will play a certain role.

00:42:48.840 --> 00:42:52.230
That said more generally list it's also

00:42:53.150 --> 00:42:56.170
an irony that most of
these illustrators are

00:42:56.170 --> 00:42:57.810
Chinese Misty source.

00:42:57.810 --> 00:43:02.060
And yet they are separating
themselves from China

00:43:02.060 --> 00:43:03.170
specifically,

00:43:03.170 --> 00:43:04.370
and trying to

00:43:06.110 --> 00:43:07.690
claim Japanese

00:43:08.900 --> 00:43:13.763
and to separate the sort of
Japanese and Chinese history,

00:43:15.604 --> 00:43:17.270
and to put Japan with Southeast Asia,

00:43:17.270 --> 00:43:18.720
rather than with East Asia,

00:43:18.720 --> 00:43:20.410
it's all really a bit confused,

00:43:20.410 --> 00:43:23.110
but in a certain way,

00:43:23.110 --> 00:43:25.430
the Chinese illustrators assimilate.

00:43:25.430 --> 00:43:29.730
So the Chinese immigrants
to the Philippines

00:43:29.730 --> 00:43:31.447
assimilate so well,

00:43:31.447 --> 00:43:34.240
and the workings of cases
are so strong there that

00:43:34.240 --> 00:43:39.240
they become a separate
group and become Filipinos.

00:43:41.120 --> 00:43:44.450
And what the Filipino Strados do

00:43:44.450 --> 00:43:47.670
is to sort of try to imitate
the Spanish denigration

00:43:47.670 --> 00:43:48.503
of the Chinese.

00:43:48.503 --> 00:43:51.030
So they have internalized
a certain kind of hierarchy

00:43:51.030 --> 00:43:52.550
for a very long time.

00:43:52.550 --> 00:43:54.361
And so in imitation of the Spanish,

00:43:54.361 --> 00:43:56.260
they tried to separate themselves

00:43:56.260 --> 00:43:59.970
so they can maintain ranking above

00:43:59.970 --> 00:44:02.040
the same way that the Spanish do

00:44:02.040 --> 00:44:05.543
and sort of ally themselves

00:44:05.543 --> 00:44:07.663
with the different kinds of Asia.

00:44:08.980 --> 00:44:11.070
They talk about cynic vise,

00:44:11.070 --> 00:44:12.630
or with regard to China

00:44:12.630 --> 00:44:16.860
and about lying and
about sort of vulgarity.

00:44:16.860 --> 00:44:20.030
And then the way that they
construct the Japanese version

00:44:20.030 --> 00:44:22.020
of Asia or the Malaysia version of Asia

00:44:22.020 --> 00:44:23.580
is very different.

00:44:23.580 --> 00:44:25.214
And they always

00:44:25.214 --> 00:44:27.755
the illustrators in
the propaganda movement

00:44:27.755 --> 00:44:30.610
have lots of essays stressing

00:44:30.610 --> 00:44:33.210
the difference between the
Japanese and the Chinese.

00:44:34.570 --> 00:44:35.403
And

00:44:37.430 --> 00:44:40.350
as to your second question about

00:44:40.350 --> 00:44:42.372
the cosmopolitan linkages guests,

