00:53:11.280 --> 00:53:14.080
And so I wanted to restore that kind of

00:53:15.120 --> 00:53:17.720
international dimension.

00:53:17.720 --> 00:53:19.620
I also thought it was
very interesting that

00:53:19.620 --> 00:53:23.280
when I looked at some of
the millenarian movements

00:53:23.280 --> 00:53:26.650
from the 1880s, 1883, 1887,

00:53:26.650 --> 00:53:29.700
there were international elements embedded

00:53:29.700 --> 00:53:32.350
within those millenarian movements.

00:53:32.350 --> 00:53:34.890
And it showed me the sort of
trans nationalized setting

00:53:34.890 --> 00:53:36.960
in which ideas of social regeneration

00:53:36.960 --> 00:53:39.130
were occurring in the
Philippines at this point.

00:53:39.130 --> 00:53:43.760
I opened the book to sort
of accounts of rumors

00:53:43.760 --> 00:53:46.210
that were spreading in the Visayas.

00:53:46.210 --> 00:53:49.920
One was this millenarian
leader named Kundalini,

00:53:49.920 --> 00:53:50.893
who said that

00:53:50.893 --> 00:53:53.710
a German steamship would come to announce

00:53:53.710 --> 00:53:56.560
that Spain did not own the bee science.

00:53:56.560 --> 00:54:00.530
And there is just how we are
God water spout who declared

00:54:01.810 --> 00:54:04.090
freedom from Spain

00:54:04.090 --> 00:54:08.450
and freed his followers
from having to pay tribute.

00:54:08.450 --> 00:54:13.450
And he was able to supposedly
able to summon rain and coins,

00:54:14.600 --> 00:54:16.420
which were from America.

00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:18.940
And so there are these
international elements

00:54:18.940 --> 00:54:21.893
that are at work with
it, fantasies and rumors,

00:54:23.531 --> 00:54:26.690
and they occur even amongst
these very localized,

00:54:26.690 --> 00:54:29.100
rural millenarian imaginings,

00:54:29.100 --> 00:54:31.310
and are not just part of sort of more

00:54:31.310 --> 00:54:34.200
cosmopolitan elites who traveled.

00:54:34.200 --> 00:54:37.420
And it's one of the reasons
why I sort of don't fetishize

00:54:37.420 --> 00:54:41.830
travel because actually there
was a lot of thinking through

00:54:41.830 --> 00:54:44.290
and world making happening locally,

00:54:44.290 --> 00:54:46.720
that involved international.

00:54:46.720 --> 00:54:50.190
And I think it's also an antidote against

00:54:50.190 --> 00:54:54.690
sort of overly binary
understandings of local and global,

00:54:54.690 --> 00:54:56.670
and the ways in which
a lot of the literature

00:54:56.670 --> 00:54:58.160
